  "scientific_assessment": [
    "Physical flow factors and spark optimum offsets are fixed plant inputs, independent of controller outputs. Their use to derive known inverse compensation is an explicit oracle fixture, not blind tuning.",
    "The plant advances a free shaft from actual delivered pulse mass and actual coil fall angle/dwell. Controller demand is diagnostic metadata and does not substitute for those delivered actuations. External Modelica MVEM is used for the hash-verified air path; combustion/free shaft are local empirical closures.",
    "The same inverse-flow percentages deliberately expose a semantic difference: the project scales effective fuel time before deadtime, while pinned production Speeduino scales the complete PW with integer percentageApprox. Keeping that case and separately labeling total-PW calibration is fair; differing arbitrary reduction thresholds are behavior assertions rather than a common performance score.",
    "Reference total-PW calibration is exactly derived from measured neutral PW3101us and fixed900us deadtime. Physical percentages [100,107.8863449,94.7424367,103.7356371] quantize to [100,108,95,104]. It is valid only at the declared operating point until separately tested elsewhere.",
    "All original late-window attempted combustion records have positive modeled work, and lambda means/CVs and physical cylinder timing independently match. Raw pulse integration agrees with per-cylinder fuel ledgers within1.2e-10mg. No late duplicate/skipped720 coil cycle was found in the new sequential runs.",
    "The rich final mixtures around0.77-0.78 establish balancing only. Both controllers use an uncalibrated common fixture, so this is not engine calibration, safe-tune validation or superiority evidence.",
    "Event metadata differs: project spark demand is latched at dwell start; reference metadata is last sampled production demand. Startup/transient error maxima must not be compared as equivalent timing-quality scores. Independently checking immutable physical TDC plus fixed late running demand gives baseline peaks0.01025deg project and0.83282deg reference."
  ],
  "remaining_nonblocking_gaps": [
    {
      "where": "tools/run_cylinder_scenarios.py:34",
      "issue": "The field named burns counts non-null-lambda attempts before the plant success filter. All current final-window attempts are successful, so current results are unaffected. Future scenarios should retain attempt/success/misfire counts separately."
    },
    {
      "where": "tools/run_cylinder_scenarios.py:66",
      "issue": "Baseline runner itself omits full edge alternation, all-channel, injector-bound and ledger assertions. The subsequent transient suite and this independent arithmetic replay cover all current cases. Preserve those dependencies when publishing a nine-case-only claim."
    },
    {
      "where": "tools/run_cylinder_scenarios.py:83",
      "issue": "Swapped negative control requires only >3x corrected spread, which becomes weak when corrected spread is tiny. Actual swapped cases are worse than disabled baseline (project0.28438 vs0.14382; reference0.34021 vs0.14456), so current negative controls are decisive. A future assertion should also compare with disabled and verify physical direction."
    },
    {
      "where": "tools/run_cylinder_transients.py:55",
      "issue": "Existing convergence metrics check final speed, total fuel and released work, not cylinder-balance metrics. Independent recaptures confirm balance at125us, but reference work CV changes from0.000984 to0.002112. Both are small; do not extend the reported<0.9% aggregate convergence claim to precise residual cylinder-spread/CV values."
    },
    {
      "where": "tools/run_cylinder_scenarios.py:87",
      "issue": "Baseline ten-source digest list does not bind all transitive parsing/phase/HAL dependencies or raw artifacts. The later43-source report and planned final artifact manifest address much of this. Keep runtime/live digest limitations explicit."
    },
    {
      "where": "tools/run_cylinder_scenarios.py:63",
      "issue": "Flat correction maps at one warm idle point do not validate an entire load/RPM trim surface or physically unequal cylinder filling. Prior gradient/native mapper tests help implementation coverage; future out-of-sample load/temperature/deadtime and independent unequal-air tests remain useful."
    }
  ],
